 minus its 0.5 km² overlap with the reserve file.</description><Style><LineStyle><color>ff5c8a1f</color><width>2</width></LineStyle><PolyStyle><color>805c8a1f</color></PolyStyle></Style><ExtendedData><Data name="layer"><value>core-added-2023</value></Data><Data name="name"><value>Core added 2023: Bhainsrorgarh WLS forest blocks</value></Data><Data name="measured_area_km2_wgs84"><value>205.47</value></Data><Data name="notified_area_km2"><value>193.09</value></Data><Data name="reliability"><value>Official sanctuary file (2018). The notification adds 12 forest blocks (193.09 km²); the file draws the whole sanctuary, so the two differ. Sanctuary area is 201.4 km² in the file's attribute but 275.45 km² in the 2021 ESZ notification.</value></Data><Data name="method"><value>Bhainsrorgarh WLS file, minus its 0.5 km² overlap with the reserve file.</value></Data><Data name="instrument"><value>Rajasthan Forest Department notification F.3(22)Forest/2023, 5 Oct 2023</value></Data><Data name="source_files"><value>Forest Department file 'Bhensrodgarh Wildlife Sanctuary.kmz'; listed as on 31.07.2018; server copy 2018-08-07; SHA-256 b670cf408245…</value></Data><Data name="source_urls"><value>https://forest.rajasthan.gov.in/content/dam/raj/forest/ForestDepartment/PDFs/Department%20Wing/Forest%20Development/Districtwise%20Forest%20Blocks%20a%20Google%20Earth/update/wildlife/Bhensrodgarh%20Wildlife%20Sanctuary.kmz</value></Data><Data name="built"><value>2026-10-23</value></Data><Data name="disclaimer"><value>Reconstructed from Rajasthan Forest Department map files for reference. Not a legal or cadastral boundary: the reserve is defined by the schedules and boundary descriptions in the notifications. The Forest Department marks its files as for management use, not legal purposes.</value></Data></ExtendedData><MultiGeometry><Polygon><outerBoundaryIs><LinearRing><coordinates>75.506978,24.793413,0 75.507162,24.793306,0 75.507500,24.793032,0 75.507600,24.792859,0 75.507633,24.792802,0 75.50